WEBVTT

00:05.255 --> 00:06.881
I don't know how to trust you.

00:08.550 --> 00:10.051
How about I keep showing you how?

00:13.054 --> 00:14.597
Don't move. Don't fucking move.

00:17.434 --> 00:20.478
Down. On your knees.
I said on your fucking knees!

00:20.478 --> 00:22.772
Watch your goddamn mouth!
I ain't some kinda--

00:27.902 --> 00:30.697
The disrespect
you have shown our family...

00:31.531 --> 00:33.408
I know about the new drug.

00:33.950 --> 00:36.703
Your lab, it's ours now.

00:36.703 --> 00:38.997
Listen, it don't have
to go down this way.

00:38.997 --> 00:40.707
You think we'd just sit by,

00:40.707 --> 00:44.085
and watch you make
excuse after excuse,

00:44.085 --> 00:45.462
and do nothing?

00:45.462 --> 00:46.921
What the fuck is she talking about?

00:46.921 --> 00:49.382
The second you walked into Blackgate,

00:49.382 --> 00:52.844
I knew you were a swindler
and a cheat.

00:52.844 --> 00:54.304
What the fuck is she talking about?

00:54.304 --> 00:55.722
Shut your goddamn mouth.

00:55.722 --> 00:58.850
Oh, I thought for a moment
you two were...

00:58.850 --> 01:00.894
that perhaps you asked him to...

01:00.894 --> 01:01.978
Asked him to what?

01:02.562 --> 01:03.938
Kill your brother...

01:04.731 --> 01:06.066
to take his place.

01:07.025 --> 01:09.110
But I'm wrong, aren't I?

01:09.944 --> 01:12.072
You didn't know.

01:16.826 --> 01:17.952
You...

01:17.952 --> 01:19.537
Nadia, you gotta listen to me.

01:20.288 --> 01:21.664
I never cheated your family.

01:21.790 --> 01:23.500
Jesus! Come on!

01:24.125 --> 01:26.002
I needed Sofia to get the new drug.

01:26.002 --> 01:27.587
All right? For us.

01:27.587 --> 01:30.131
It's yours. It's fucking yours!
I was gonna bring it to you.

01:30.131 --> 01:31.716
I swear to God. You gotta trust me.

01:31.716 --> 01:33.093
I'm on your side.

01:46.189 --> 01:47.065
Let's go!

01:56.032 --> 01:56.991
Get in!

02:05.250 --> 02:06.960
- Sofia?
- Julian.

02:07.460 --> 02:09.796
I need... I need help.

02:09.796 --> 02:11.006
Where are you?

02:12.924 --> 02:15.218
It was... It...

02:15.218 --> 02:17.595
It was... Oz.

02:17.595 --> 02:18.680
Sofia?

02:20.682 --> 02:21.641
Sofia?

02:23.685 --> 02:24.519
Sofia?!

02:27.022 --> 02:29.024
On behalf of the Lucy House,

02:29.024 --> 02:32.318
it is my pleasure
to welcome the chairwoman

02:32.318 --> 02:35.572
of the Isabella Falcone Foundation,

02:35.572 --> 02:37.657
Sofia Falcone.

02:54.758 --> 02:58.219
I've never been one
for speeches, but...

03:00.096 --> 03:04.517
my mother, Isabella Falcone,

03:04.517 --> 03:07.771
struggled with depression for years.

03:08.938 --> 03:11.274
She never got the help
that she needed,

03:11.274 --> 03:13.777
and when I was nine,

03:14.944 --> 03:16.613
she took her own life.

03:18.239 --> 03:20.658
That's why my father and I
started this foundation.

03:20.658 --> 03:23.953
We wanted to support charities
like this one

03:23.953 --> 03:28.291
that provide women and girls
with life-saving services.

03:31.503 --> 03:34.798
I'm so busy with our gala
and our golf tournament next month.

03:34.798 --> 03:36.424
- Great speech.
- Thank you.

03:36.424 --> 03:38.385
Sofia, you will be there,
won't you? It is so fun.

03:38.385 --> 03:39.719
Yes. I'm so sorry. I have to run.

03:39.719 --> 03:41.096
- Thank you.
- Thank you, Mrs. Hill.

03:41.096 --> 03:42.889
You need a cigarette,
take the edge off?

03:42.889 --> 03:44.557
This is the third luncheon this week.

03:44.557 --> 03:46.309
A lobotomy
couldn't take the edge off.

03:46.309 --> 03:48.353
I'm sure your father appreciates it.

03:48.353 --> 03:50.105
But yeah, even when
you're helping people,

03:50.105 --> 03:51.898
you still gotta eat shit.

03:51.898 --> 03:53.525
It's better than some jobs, though.

03:54.567 --> 03:56.528
Yeah, like what? Driving me around?

03:56.528 --> 03:58.613
Nah, that ain't...
You know what I mean.

03:58.613 --> 04:00.031
Oz, I'm messing with you.

04:00.031 --> 04:01.741
It's a shitty job, I know.

04:01.741 --> 04:03.284
You deserve better.

04:03.868 --> 04:05.954
I mean, we both do,
but... you have a dick,

04:05.954 --> 04:08.164
so at least you're eligible
for a promotion.

04:11.793 --> 04:13.003
I'll get the car.

04:13.503 --> 04:14.796
- You did good.
- Thank you.

04:14.796 --> 04:15.922
Ms. Falcone.

04:16.715 --> 04:18.883
I know you're on your way out,
but do you have a minute?

04:21.219 --> 04:22.262
Sorry. Of course, yes.

04:22.262 --> 04:23.346
- I'm Summer Gleeson.
- Hi.

04:23.346 --> 04:25.348
I've been following your work
with the Foundation.

04:25.348 --> 04:26.975
- It's impressive.
- Thank you.

04:26.975 --> 04:29.644
But if you don't mind me saying,
I think you could be doing more.

04:29.644 --> 04:30.854
I don't know if you're aware,

04:30.854 --> 04:33.189
but a young woman named Yolanda Jones

04:33.189 --> 04:34.733
committed suicide last week.

04:34.733 --> 04:37.277
There's actually been
a number of women like Ms. Jones

04:37.277 --> 04:39.696
over the last decade,
and they all died the same way,

04:40.530 --> 04:41.364
by hanging.

04:42.032 --> 04:43.533
Which... that's how your mother died

04:43.533 --> 04:45.035
if I'm not mistaken.

04:46.327 --> 04:47.746
I'm sorry. I don't mean to--

04:47.746 --> 04:49.622
You said there was something
I could do to help.

04:50.290 --> 04:52.417
Yolanda Jones worked
at the Iceberg Lounge.

04:52.417 --> 04:54.753
In fact, most of these women
worked for businesses

04:54.753 --> 04:56.087
owned by your father.

04:57.172 --> 04:59.466
What organization
did you say you were with?

05:02.761 --> 05:03.845
I don't talk to press.

05:04.346 --> 05:06.056
- Sofia, please.
- I don't talk to press.

05:06.056 --> 05:08.725
Hey! Back off, lady.
She don't wanna talk to you.

05:09.726 --> 05:11.353
More women could get hurt.

05:13.855 --> 05:15.023
You could help them.

05:24.741 --> 05:25.825
You okay, Sofia?

05:28.411 --> 05:30.455
Ready or not, here I come!

05:30.455 --> 05:32.582
Alberto, I know you're in here.

05:35.710 --> 05:37.837
Alberto, where are you?

05:52.727 --> 05:53.561
Mom?

06:03.446 --> 06:05.323
Sofia, how was your luncheon?

06:06.741 --> 06:07.659
Good.

06:12.372 --> 06:13.623
Ruth sends her regards.

06:14.290 --> 06:15.500
Which one's Ruth?

06:16.042 --> 06:17.502
The wife of Congressman Hill...

06:19.504 --> 06:22.215
who's finally taking my calls,
thanks to your sister.

06:27.804 --> 06:29.222
Right. Hill.

06:32.142 --> 06:34.644
I asked you to look into
his financial holdings.

06:36.312 --> 06:37.313
I'm working on it.

06:37.814 --> 06:39.024
I've been busy,

06:39.024 --> 06:41.192
but tomorrow, I promise.

06:42.402 --> 06:44.571
Why are you such a fool
when your sister's so reliable?

06:44.571 --> 06:46.156
I know, Pop.

06:46.156 --> 06:47.532
I get it. I'm sorry.

06:51.202 --> 06:52.203
Shit!

06:52.203 --> 06:54.289
I gotta go.

07:05.759 --> 07:07.594
I don't know what to do with him.

07:09.512 --> 07:10.472
The drinking...

07:11.389 --> 07:12.307
the partying.

07:13.892 --> 07:16.102
I can't have your brother
embarrassing me next weekend,

07:16.102 --> 07:17.562
not with the Family flying in.

07:17.562 --> 07:19.981
I'm gonna watch him.
I'll make sure that he behaves.

07:21.149 --> 07:22.233
Thank you, beautiful.

07:25.904 --> 07:27.447
You know, he's not like you and me.

07:29.366 --> 07:30.241
He's soft.

07:37.457 --> 07:40.085
I've been thinking recently
about the future...

07:41.378 --> 07:43.213
about our Family's future.

07:44.005 --> 07:45.799
Maybe it's time
to break with tradition.

07:46.883 --> 07:48.009
When the time comes,

07:49.135 --> 07:50.470
I want you to take my place.

07:53.473 --> 07:54.974
I want you to run this Family...

07:56.393 --> 07:58.186
if that's something
that would interest you.

07:58.186 --> 07:59.729
Yeah.

08:00.522 --> 08:01.481
Yeah, of course.

08:02.190 --> 08:04.651
I would be... honored.

08:06.778 --> 08:07.946
But the rest of the Family--

08:07.946 --> 08:10.073
They know you're mine.
They'll do as I say.

08:15.745 --> 08:16.746
What? What is it?

08:18.790 --> 08:19.666
Tell me.

08:21.960 --> 08:22.794
Oh, it's nothing.

08:29.384 --> 08:30.218
I don't know.

08:32.220 --> 08:33.722
Maybe it's because of the Foundation,

08:33.722 --> 08:37.934
but I've just been...
thinking a lot about Mom.

08:50.030 --> 08:52.198
I know I was so young, but I...

08:53.742 --> 08:54.659
It's just...

08:55.368 --> 08:58.413
I don't remember her being sick

08:59.164 --> 09:00.373
or depressed.

09:01.249 --> 09:02.792
She was good at hiding it.

09:05.503 --> 09:08.048
Look, I miss her too, baby,
every day.

09:08.590 --> 09:12.302
Did she ever see anyone before...

09:12.802 --> 09:15.347
Like a therapist or a psychiatrist?

09:18.600 --> 09:20.143
Your mother was a proud woman...

09:21.728 --> 09:22.729
stubborn.

09:24.731 --> 09:26.149
She refused my help,

09:26.775 --> 09:28.902
as much as I tried, and...

09:29.944 --> 09:31.237
God knows I tried.

09:31.821 --> 09:33.114
Of course, yeah.

09:36.409 --> 09:38.161
- I just--
- Sofia.

09:40.914 --> 09:42.207
Why would you do this now?

09:44.376 --> 09:46.044
Picking away at old wounds...

09:46.544 --> 09:48.213
You know how it upsets me.

09:48.213 --> 09:50.840
I'm sorry. I didn't mean to.

09:59.265 --> 10:01.601
You still haven't told me
what you want for your birthday.

10:07.565 --> 10:09.484
I'm sure I'll love it,
whatever you get me.

10:20.620 --> 10:21.579
Don't worry.

10:24.124 --> 10:25.625
Pop's gonna lose his shit over it.

10:25.625 --> 10:26.751
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

10:26.751 --> 10:27.794
How do you know?

10:27.794 --> 10:30.380
'Cause it's old and expensive,
like his favorite child.

10:31.881 --> 10:32.924
Shit!

10:33.717 --> 10:35.969
Your Penguin up there
is gonna have to clean this up.

10:35.969 --> 10:36.886
Don't call him that.

10:37.470 --> 10:39.556
- You'll take care of the card?
- Yeah.

10:40.306 --> 10:42.434
Wait. Can I ask you something?

10:43.476 --> 10:45.729
The girls at the 44 Below,

10:45.729 --> 10:49.691
has Dad ever had relationships
with them?

10:52.027 --> 10:54.487
Those girls aren't exactly
the relationship type.

10:55.655 --> 10:58.116
Since when do you care
about Pop's love life?

10:58.116 --> 10:59.492
It's been a long time since Mom,

10:59.492 --> 11:02.120
and he doesn't really talk to me
about it, and...

11:02.746 --> 11:04.956
I don't know. You get to see
a whole 'nother side of him.

11:04.956 --> 11:06.875
- What side? He's Pop.
- Yeah, I know.

11:06.875 --> 11:09.753
But you know what I mean.
It's very different with me.

11:11.338 --> 11:13.340
I just thought
you might have seen something.

11:14.591 --> 11:15.925
What are you asking?

11:15.925 --> 11:17.260
I guess I...

11:18.720 --> 11:20.221
Sometimes, I wonder if I...

11:21.681 --> 11:22.515
really...

11:24.017 --> 11:25.185
really know him.

11:25.852 --> 11:28.188
Like, with all the lies
that we had to tell growing up

11:28.188 --> 11:30.231
about what he does, and there's...

11:30.231 --> 11:32.025
there's a lot
that we don't talk about.

11:33.526 --> 11:35.111
There is something, but...

11:37.947 --> 11:39.699
I can't. He'd fucking kill me.

11:43.995 --> 11:45.413
Pop's...

11:45.413 --> 11:46.498
Mossad,

11:47.332 --> 11:49.334
and the girls at the club
are trained female assassins.

11:49.334 --> 11:50.543
Shut up!

11:51.211 --> 11:53.797
Listen, whatever
you're thinking, don't.

11:53.797 --> 11:56.675
What Pop does at work,
he does at work.

11:57.592 --> 12:01.137
I mean, we got a good life, right?

12:07.435 --> 12:08.561
Where to, Sofia?

12:19.948 --> 12:20.990
This is everything.

12:21.866 --> 12:23.201
Coroner reports are consistent.

12:23.201 --> 12:26.621
They all died from asphyxia.

12:26.621 --> 12:28.164
I'm not disputing that.

12:28.164 --> 12:29.791
What I find strange is,

12:29.791 --> 12:31.042
according to the police,

12:31.042 --> 12:34.587
official cause of death
is suicide by hanging.

12:35.880 --> 12:38.049
Do you see the impressions
around the neck?

12:38.591 --> 12:41.469
They're far more congruent
with manual strangulation.

12:41.469 --> 12:42.762
Like someone's hands?

12:43.346 --> 12:44.305
Exactly.

12:44.889 --> 12:46.641
Then there's the defensive wounds.

12:46.641 --> 12:48.685
They were left off
the police reports.

12:49.477 --> 12:51.271
You can see these women,
they fought back.

12:51.271 --> 12:52.981
Biting, scratching... They--

12:52.981 --> 12:54.566
Why are you telling me this?

12:56.818 --> 12:59.112
I need access to the girls
working at the club.

12:59.696 --> 13:00.739
It's not exclusive.

13:00.739 --> 13:02.991
Not the Iceberg Lounge, the 44 Below,

13:02.991 --> 13:05.326
where Yolanda Jones actually worked.

13:06.327 --> 13:08.371
- If you wore a wire--
- To my father's club?

13:09.039 --> 13:10.123
Never gonna happen.

13:10.123 --> 13:12.375
Then just give me access
to employee records.

13:12.500 --> 13:13.710
Women who are new in town,

13:13.710 --> 13:16.379
who don't have
family or friends close by,

13:16.379 --> 13:18.006
the type whose death or disappearance

13:18.006 --> 13:19.382
doesn't make the news.

13:20.133 --> 13:21.801
We need to protect these women.

13:23.470 --> 13:24.387
Mom?

13:31.019 --> 13:33.271
Oh, no. No. Sofia.

13:35.106 --> 13:36.274
Don't look.

13:37.734 --> 13:38.651
Don't look.

13:40.028 --> 13:40.862
Dad.

13:44.574 --> 13:45.533
Sofia?

13:47.327 --> 13:49.079
Sofia, what is it?

13:51.289 --> 13:52.457
This is all you have?

13:53.124 --> 13:54.125
That's it?

13:54.125 --> 13:58.088
Just, like, some old reports
and conspiracy theories?

13:58.088 --> 13:59.339
It's ridiculous.

14:00.256 --> 14:01.841
And it reeks

14:01.841 --> 14:04.678
of a junior reporter
desperate for a byline.

14:04.678 --> 14:05.762
Sofia, please, just--

14:05.762 --> 14:08.264
You don't know shit about my father.

14:08.264 --> 14:10.433
He is a good man!

14:11.518 --> 14:13.687
And if you try publishing
any of this garbage,

14:13.687 --> 14:16.147
my family will destroy you.

14:17.565 --> 14:18.900
Do you understand?

14:37.335 --> 14:39.129
That the same lady from the luncheon?

14:40.630 --> 14:42.257
Look, Sofia, meeting a reporter...

14:43.049 --> 14:44.926
people are gonna start to get ideas.

14:44.926 --> 14:46.052
Your father might not like--

14:46.052 --> 14:46.970
Oz, stop!

14:48.972 --> 14:50.974
Stop talking.

14:50.974 --> 14:52.308
I don't need your advice.

14:52.308 --> 14:55.395
I don't care what you think.
No one does.

14:55.395 --> 14:57.022
You are my driver.
That is all you are.

14:57.022 --> 14:58.648
So stop talking and drive.

15:16.750 --> 15:17.751
Sofia!

15:19.753 --> 15:20.962
Sofia.

15:20.962 --> 15:23.340
- Carla!
- Aw, Sofia! Thank God!

15:24.174 --> 15:26.634
Have you seen bride number three?

15:28.762 --> 15:30.013
- Oh, my God.
- It's a lot.

15:30.013 --> 15:31.097
It's a lot.

15:31.097 --> 15:33.016
Yeah.

15:33.016 --> 15:35.101
Luca says he met her in Portugal.

15:35.101 --> 15:36.019
Okay.

15:38.521 --> 15:39.939
Portugal.com.

15:41.316 --> 15:42.150
Yeah.

15:42.650 --> 15:45.070
You must catch me up
on absolutely everything.

15:45.070 --> 15:46.905
- Oh my God, yeah. Absolutely.
- Everything.

15:46.905 --> 15:48.865
- First, a martini?
- Obviously.

15:50.158 --> 15:51.785
Sofia. Hey.

15:52.327 --> 15:53.953
Oz, what are you doing inside?

15:56.289 --> 15:57.207
Is that a new jacket?

15:57.207 --> 15:58.166
Yeah.

15:59.042 --> 16:00.877
- Looks good.
- Thank you.

16:00.877 --> 16:02.462
Your father wants to see you.

16:03.213 --> 16:04.214
He's in his office.

16:29.447 --> 16:31.616
Don't tell me you're sick
of the party already.

16:32.575 --> 16:35.161
Uncle Luca hasn't even told
his vasectomy story yet.

16:35.161 --> 16:37.247
Why didn't you tell me
you met with a reporter?

16:37.247 --> 16:41.334
You never, ever talk to the press.

16:42.877 --> 16:44.087
I thought you understood that.

16:44.713 --> 16:45.880
Did Oz tell you that?

16:47.549 --> 16:50.176
Oz doesn't know
what he's talking about.

16:50.176 --> 16:53.430
Some woman approached me,
but I told her to fuck off.

16:53.430 --> 16:54.347
That's it.

16:54.347 --> 16:55.598
Is that right?

16:57.142 --> 16:58.059
Yeah.

16:58.560 --> 16:59.519
Dad...

17:01.187 --> 17:02.772
I spoke to Kenzie.

17:02.772 --> 17:06.109
Summer Gleeson has been working
with the police.

17:07.736 --> 17:09.571
There's an open investigation.

17:11.072 --> 17:12.657
They're looking into me for murder.

17:14.659 --> 17:16.202
Murder, Sofia.

17:17.328 --> 17:18.955
Some hookers at the club.

17:21.416 --> 17:23.877
- Why didn't you come to me?
- I should have. You're right.

17:23.877 --> 17:27.047
But I knew that it was bullshit,
and I didn't wanna worry you.

17:27.047 --> 17:27.964
Stop.

17:29.257 --> 17:31.009
Do you think I did these things?

17:32.093 --> 17:33.470
No, of course not.

17:33.470 --> 17:35.263
You were supposed
to be better than this.

17:36.222 --> 17:37.057
This...

17:38.016 --> 17:39.017
was meant for you.

17:41.144 --> 17:42.103
All of it.

17:43.104 --> 17:44.356
How could you do this to me?

17:44.898 --> 17:47.359
I didn't... I've never...

17:48.485 --> 17:50.028
I've never doubted you.

17:51.613 --> 17:52.447
I love you.

17:53.198 --> 17:55.575
And I know that there is
an explanation.

17:56.326 --> 17:57.744
An explanation for what?

18:01.998 --> 18:04.459
You had scratches on your hands

18:05.168 --> 18:06.544
the day Mom died.

18:12.425 --> 18:15.804
But I know they weren't from her.

18:15.804 --> 18:17.681
I know that. I...

18:19.391 --> 18:20.350
They were from...

18:22.185 --> 18:23.645
something else. I...

18:23.645 --> 18:25.313
I don't know what, but...

18:27.357 --> 18:29.025
Something.

18:39.911 --> 18:40.995
Right?

18:47.377 --> 18:48.378
My...

18:49.796 --> 18:51.172
sweet Sofia.

18:53.591 --> 18:54.759
What has happened to you?

18:57.762 --> 18:59.180
You're clearly not yourself.

19:00.849 --> 19:04.060
You're confused, sick.

19:07.230 --> 19:09.149
I think you need to leave
before you make a scene.

19:12.485 --> 19:14.112
Dad, please--

19:14.237 --> 19:15.488
Oz will drive you home.

19:16.740 --> 19:17.574
Now.

19:29.002 --> 19:30.712
Listen, I get that you're angry,
you know.

19:30.712 --> 19:32.172
But I was just doing my job,

19:32.881 --> 19:33.965
looking out for you.

19:33.965 --> 19:35.967
That's what your father pays me for.

19:36.551 --> 19:38.303
These reporters,
they get in your head.

19:38.303 --> 19:40.055
- You can't trust 'em.
- Jesus, Oz, shut up!

19:40.055 --> 19:41.639
If you were really looking out
for me,

19:41.639 --> 19:44.309
you would've talked to me, not him.

19:45.977 --> 19:47.228
I trusted you.

19:49.981 --> 19:52.442
Congratulations.
You got what you wanted.

19:53.193 --> 19:54.444
My father sees you now.

19:55.278 --> 19:58.239
You and everyone you love
is on his radar.

19:59.949 --> 20:02.577
Come on. What the fuck is this?

20:13.713 --> 20:15.632
Come on, Kenzie. You wanna kill
the circus lights?

20:15.632 --> 20:18.051
I'm taking Ms. Falcone home.
Father's orders.

20:20.178 --> 20:22.222
Ms. Falcone, step outside.

20:22.722 --> 20:24.974
- What is this?
- Did my dad call you?

20:24.974 --> 20:26.518
Step out of the car.

20:26.518 --> 20:28.937
Oh, my God. Are you kidding me?

20:33.149 --> 20:34.192
Sofia Falcone.

20:35.360 --> 20:36.861
- Get off me. Wait!
- You're under arrest

20:36.861 --> 20:38.530
for the murder of Summer Gleeson.

20:38.530 --> 20:40.281
- The reporter?
- What?!

20:40.865 --> 20:42.742
Did you do this? For him?

20:42.742 --> 20:44.619
No. I got no idea
what the fuck is going on.

20:44.619 --> 20:46.538
- Kenzie, what the fuck?
- You're also being charged

20:46.538 --> 20:48.081
with the murder of Yolanda Jones,

20:48.081 --> 20:49.666
Taylor Montgomery, and Nancy Hoffman.

20:49.666 --> 20:51.918
- Get out of here with that!
- No, I didn't kill anyone!

20:51.918 --> 20:54.004
Oz, you gotta do something!

20:54.004 --> 20:55.755
Hey, let her go!

20:55.755 --> 20:57.924
Take my advice
and shut the fuck up, Penguin.

20:57.924 --> 20:59.050
Oz, call Alberto!

20:59.968 --> 21:01.678
Stop! Call Alberto!

21:01.678 --> 21:04.806
- Get your fucking hands off--
- Tell him what's going on! Oz!

21:08.184 --> 21:09.060
The Hangman?

21:09.811 --> 21:11.479
That's what they're calling me?

21:11.479 --> 21:13.523
It's just tabloid bullshit.
It'll pass.

21:13.523 --> 21:15.734
Sofia, your father's claiming

21:15.734 --> 21:17.485
that you have a history
of mental illness.

21:17.485 --> 21:18.820
Well, that's ridiculous.

21:18.820 --> 21:20.363
The ADA met with the judge,

21:20.363 --> 21:22.949
and the court has ordered
a psychological evaluation.

21:22.949 --> 21:24.367
Because my dad said so?

21:24.367 --> 21:25.827
It's not just your father.

21:25.827 --> 21:28.788
A number of family members
have written affidavits

21:28.788 --> 21:30.248
suggesting the same.

21:30.248 --> 21:31.958
Your uncle Luca.

21:31.958 --> 21:34.377
Your cousins Johnny and Carla Viti.

21:34.377 --> 21:36.921
They're using
my mother's suicide as a...

21:39.341 --> 21:41.760
I have a compulsion
for killing animals?

21:41.760 --> 21:43.636
Are you fucking serious?

21:44.137 --> 21:46.514
- Did you know about this?
- No. I swear.

21:49.392 --> 21:50.643
So, I...

21:50.643 --> 21:52.812
I do an evaluation, and I...

21:52.812 --> 21:55.607
answer a few questions
to prove I'm sane, right?

21:55.607 --> 21:57.525
That's it, right? Then what?

21:57.525 --> 21:59.402
I'm afraid it's not that simple.

21:59.402 --> 22:02.364
The judge agreed
to the ADA's request.

22:02.364 --> 22:04.908
You're being remanded
to Arkham State Hospital

22:04.908 --> 22:05.950
for observation.

22:05.950 --> 22:07.285
No.

22:07.869 --> 22:09.788
No. That doesn't make any sense.

22:09.788 --> 22:12.707
You'll be under their care
till the start of trial.

22:12.707 --> 22:14.000
When is that?

22:14.000 --> 22:15.335
Six months from now.

22:16.002 --> 22:17.379
- Oh, my God!
- I'm sorry.

22:17.379 --> 22:19.214
No. I'm not doing that.

22:20.298 --> 22:21.841
I am not doing that.

22:23.718 --> 22:26.471
Can't you stop this?
You're my fucking lawyer!

22:26.471 --> 22:27.472
I'm sorry.

22:29.099 --> 22:30.308
I'll give you two a minute.

22:33.770 --> 22:36.648
He is punishing me
for something he did.

22:36.648 --> 22:37.816
You don't know that.

22:37.816 --> 22:40.819
Alberto, wake up!
Are you kidding me?!

22:41.403 --> 22:42.862
He strangled those women,

22:42.862 --> 22:44.781
and then he strangled that reporter

22:44.781 --> 22:46.950
and strung her up to pin it on me.

22:47.826 --> 22:49.452
He did the same thing to Mom.

22:50.203 --> 22:52.038
It's true. And I'm not gonna make it.

22:52.038 --> 22:54.624
I'm not gonna make it
in a place like that.

22:54.624 --> 22:56.292
I'm gonna die in there.

22:56.835 --> 22:59.546
I'm gonna die in there,
and he knows it. He knows it.

22:59.546 --> 23:01.172
- That's what he wants.
- Stop.

23:02.132 --> 23:03.675
It's only six months.

23:03.675 --> 23:05.719
You can handle six months.

23:05.719 --> 23:07.887
And then you're gonna get a trial,

23:07.887 --> 23:09.139
and you're gonna get out.

23:09.139 --> 23:10.265
You are, God damn it.

23:10.265 --> 23:11.725
- I promise you.
- It's time.

23:13.852 --> 23:15.020
Wait. Right now?

23:15.603 --> 23:18.273
Listen, you're a fucking Falcone.

23:18.273 --> 23:19.232
You can do this.

23:19.232 --> 23:21.568
- I know you can.
- No. Wait. Stop.

23:21.568 --> 23:22.986
Please, stop. Please.

23:22.986 --> 23:24.237
Sofia!

23:24.237 --> 23:26.531
- Please!
- Sofia, it's gonna be okay.

23:26.531 --> 23:27.490
Alberto!

23:28.074 --> 23:29.367
Don't let him win.

23:30.285 --> 23:32.245
Please. Alberto!

24:21.961 --> 24:23.963
Falcone, Sofia.

24:24.464 --> 24:26.800
I'm Dr. Ventris, chief psychiatrist.

24:26.800 --> 24:29.511
I'll be overseeing your care
for the next six months.

24:29.511 --> 24:32.764
This is my associate,
Dr. Julian Rush.

24:32.764 --> 24:35.392
He'll be conducting
the psychological evaluation.

24:35.392 --> 24:38.770
While you're here, you'll be under
court-ordered mandatory isolation,

24:38.770 --> 24:40.814
which means no visitors,
no outside contact.

24:40.814 --> 24:41.940
Wait, what?

24:41.940 --> 24:44.734
It's important for us
to observe you without interference.

24:44.734 --> 24:46.695
No. Wait! Wait a second!

24:46.695 --> 24:48.905
There's been a mistake here, okay?

24:48.905 --> 24:51.157
And I know-- Stop. Please, just...

24:51.157 --> 24:52.701
I know that people say that
all the time,

24:52.701 --> 24:54.119
but it is true, all right?

24:54.119 --> 24:57.122
I am innocent! Please!

24:57.122 --> 24:59.499
I realize this is
a difficult adjustment.

25:06.381 --> 25:07.215
Shall we?

25:18.018 --> 25:19.102
Follow me.

25:41.291 --> 25:42.500
Get some rest.

26:07.692 --> 26:08.735
Hi.

26:10.403 --> 26:11.279
Hello.

26:12.530 --> 26:13.406
Up here.

26:21.039 --> 26:22.040
Lights out!

26:24.334 --> 26:26.127
You're the Hangman, aren't you?

26:27.170 --> 26:29.381
I saw you on the TV.

26:31.800 --> 26:33.635
My name is Magpie.

26:34.135 --> 26:35.011
Like the bird.

26:36.805 --> 26:38.056
Not "Margaret."

26:38.056 --> 26:40.058
My stepmom
used to call me "Margaret,"

26:40.058 --> 26:42.310
and I told her not to,
and she didn't listen.

26:45.855 --> 26:49.192
It's okay to be scared.
I was scared at first, too,

26:49.192 --> 26:52.987
but it's not so bad here.
You get used to the noises.

26:52.987 --> 26:54.406
I'm getting out in six months.

26:54.406 --> 26:55.865
Isn't that exciting?

26:55.865 --> 26:58.827
Ooh, I bet there'll be
lots of paparazzi at your trial.

26:58.827 --> 27:01.663
No one even wrote about mine.

27:01.663 --> 27:05.000
Is it fun being famous?
Oh, I bet it's fun.

27:06.167 --> 27:08.253
Hangman?

27:09.713 --> 27:12.257
Hangman...

27:17.053 --> 27:19.055
Check out the new chick.

27:24.728 --> 27:26.521
Hangman.

27:29.190 --> 27:30.775
Hey, pretty lady.

27:35.405 --> 27:36.239
Hangman.

27:37.073 --> 27:38.908
Hangman! It's me, Magpie.

27:38.908 --> 27:40.118
I saved you a seat.

27:47.250 --> 27:49.753
Dr. V says it's important
that I make friends.

27:50.628 --> 27:52.797
Sometimes, I have a problem
with that.

27:53.882 --> 27:55.300
But I'm making progress.

27:58.386 --> 27:59.429
Candy!

28:01.639 --> 28:02.474
What is that?

28:07.687 --> 28:10.190
You only get it when you're good.

28:30.251 --> 28:32.962
What is she--
Shouldn't she be chained?

28:38.468 --> 28:40.553
Hey.

28:40.553 --> 28:43.682
Wow! Do you see that? The colors?

28:44.557 --> 28:46.142
It's all so shiny.

28:46.142 --> 28:49.354
Hey, she's not... She not chained.

28:52.982 --> 28:55.652
You killed those girls.

28:56.528 --> 28:59.739
Girls. Girls. Girls.

29:02.867 --> 29:04.244
I didn't kill anyone.

29:04.244 --> 29:05.620
You're lying.

29:07.497 --> 29:11.209
She's lying! Lying. Lying. Lying.

29:20.677 --> 29:24.514
You killed them!
Say it! Say it! Say it!

29:50.999 --> 29:52.375
How are you feeling?

29:52.375 --> 29:55.670
I heard you had an incident
in the mess hall today.

29:56.379 --> 29:58.423
A woman beat the shit out of me

29:58.423 --> 30:00.300
while everyone stood around
and watched.

30:00.300 --> 30:02.302
So, yeah, I had an incident. Yeah.

30:03.428 --> 30:04.846
I'm sorry that happened to you.

30:06.431 --> 30:09.309
Why was she unchained?

30:09.976 --> 30:11.019
I don't know.

30:11.978 --> 30:13.063
They're looking into it.

30:14.731 --> 30:16.816
Did someone release her?

30:16.816 --> 30:18.151
Is that what you believe?

30:18.651 --> 30:20.445
The attack in there was coordinated?

30:23.615 --> 30:26.326
- I know what you're doing.
- What's that?

30:26.326 --> 30:29.245
You're twisting my words around
to make me sound paranoid.

30:29.913 --> 30:31.039
But you weren't there.

30:31.039 --> 30:33.500
Someone had to have set her free.

30:37.837 --> 30:39.839
You've been in therapy before, I see.

30:39.839 --> 30:41.841
With Dr. Shaw.

30:43.051 --> 30:44.135
After your mother died.

30:48.556 --> 30:51.685
The death of a parent
is a traumatic event,

30:51.685 --> 30:53.436
and it's not unusual

30:53.436 --> 30:56.606
to transfer that grief into anger

30:57.524 --> 30:58.400
or even violence.

30:58.400 --> 31:02.278
It's not unusual
to just be sad, either.

31:02.779 --> 31:03.697
Right?

31:04.781 --> 31:06.157
I didn't kill those women.

31:07.492 --> 31:09.202
I would never do anything like that.

31:11.371 --> 31:12.497
I am here

31:13.248 --> 31:18.253
because my father
wants to keep me quiet,

31:18.253 --> 31:20.171
and my family will do
whatever he says.

31:20.171 --> 31:21.840
So you're saying that your father

31:22.757 --> 31:24.217
framed you for murder?

31:27.137 --> 31:28.304
You don't believe me.

31:29.097 --> 31:30.181
I didn't say that.

31:30.890 --> 31:32.225
I can tell.

31:35.353 --> 31:37.439
I don't know
how to convince you I'm sane

31:37.439 --> 31:39.816
when you've already made up
your mind about me.

31:41.192 --> 31:42.485
I'm here to help you, Sofia.

31:44.112 --> 31:45.655
I have no other agenda than that.

32:04.299 --> 32:05.133
Move!

32:30.950 --> 32:33.661
Fuck you, bitch! Bitch! Bitch!

32:35.580 --> 32:37.415
Come here so I can eat
your fucking mouth.

32:37.415 --> 32:39.042
Mouth. Mouth. Mouth.

32:41.670 --> 32:43.004
Come on, try it.

32:43.004 --> 32:45.757
Try it. Try it. Try it.

32:56.685 --> 32:58.061
You want me to hurt her.

32:58.812 --> 32:59.938
Right?

32:59.938 --> 33:03.274
To what? Prove I'm a killer?
Is that it?

33:03.274 --> 33:06.528
You killed them.
Say it! Say it! Say it!

33:08.988 --> 33:09.989
This is my father.

33:09.989 --> 33:12.867
You're working for him.

33:22.252 --> 33:23.211
End it.

33:24.045 --> 33:25.505
Please. End it.

33:25.505 --> 33:26.548
End it.

33:27.298 --> 33:28.508
End it.

33:30.719 --> 33:33.013
End it! End it!

33:36.850 --> 33:38.560
What happened?

33:41.938 --> 33:43.314
What are you doing?

33:43.982 --> 33:45.942
No, no. What is that?

33:46.776 --> 33:47.819
It's set.

33:47.819 --> 33:50.363
You can't do this.
I didn't do anything wrong.

33:50.488 --> 33:53.783
This isn't a punishment.
You're agitated, confused.

33:54.492 --> 33:56.244
This'll help you feel
like yourself again.

33:56.244 --> 33:57.746
- Wait.
- Open wide.

33:57.746 --> 33:58.955
No!

33:58.955 --> 34:00.040
Open!

34:18.433 --> 34:19.351
Hangman?

34:20.560 --> 34:21.603
Are you okay?

34:39.245 --> 34:40.163
What?

34:45.126 --> 34:47.128
Why are you doing this?

34:47.879 --> 34:49.631
I'm innocent.

35:09.150 --> 35:10.318
I didn't kill anyone!

35:11.903 --> 35:13.488
Stop!

35:13.488 --> 35:14.656
Please!

35:16.157 --> 35:17.826
What if she's telling the truth?

35:19.411 --> 35:20.954
Careful, Doctor.

36:08.251 --> 36:09.252
Mom?

36:25.143 --> 36:26.186
Sofia.

36:26.770 --> 36:27.729
You've got a visitor.

36:31.191 --> 36:32.192
Go on.

36:39.240 --> 36:40.950
- Alberto.
- Sofia.

36:46.331 --> 36:47.999
- Sofia.
- What?

36:47.999 --> 36:50.168
Fuck! I'm so sorry.

36:51.503 --> 36:52.796
You're not going to court.

36:54.005 --> 36:55.507
No one's gonna hear your case.

36:55.507 --> 36:58.343
Your doctor, he's claiming
you're unfit to stand trial.

36:58.343 --> 36:59.594
Dr. Rush?

37:00.220 --> 37:01.846
He wouldn't do that.

37:01.846 --> 37:04.974
It was the head of Arkham.
Some guy named Ventris.

37:05.767 --> 37:08.436
He wrote the report,
and the judge agreed. It's done.

37:10.313 --> 37:11.147
But that's...

37:12.982 --> 37:13.817
That's not...

37:14.693 --> 37:16.444
I did my six months.

37:17.946 --> 37:20.156
I deserve a trial. I...

37:20.156 --> 37:22.409
I have... rights.

37:22.409 --> 37:23.576
This is my life.

37:23.576 --> 37:25.161
We'll file an appeal.

37:25.161 --> 37:27.622
Or try for a new evaluation.

37:28.248 --> 37:30.750
I don't know. Tell me
what to do, and I'll do it.

37:30.750 --> 37:31.876
- That's it.
- No.

37:33.545 --> 37:34.796
Sofia...

37:35.714 --> 37:38.675
Sofia, no, don't. Don't. Please.

37:39.259 --> 37:42.262
I know this is fucked,
but you gotta keep fighting.

37:43.263 --> 37:44.556
I'm not giving up.

37:47.267 --> 37:49.769
I swear to God, one day,
I'll get you out of here.

37:51.271 --> 37:52.105
Sofia.

37:54.816 --> 37:55.817
Sofia!

37:57.777 --> 37:58.862
Sofia!

38:08.538 --> 38:11.541
Sofia. I didn't know Ventris
was gonna write the report.

38:12.125 --> 38:13.293
I tried to stop him.

38:16.254 --> 38:17.088
I'm sorry.

38:18.465 --> 38:19.341
How'd it go?

38:21.593 --> 38:23.845
Uh-oh. Not good?

38:24.888 --> 38:27.974
Well, at least
we can stay friends now.

38:29.059 --> 38:30.018
Best friends.

38:31.644 --> 38:33.813
And I can show the garden.

38:34.689 --> 38:37.275
There aren't any plants, though.
It's more of a yard, really.

38:37.275 --> 38:40.028
I always look for birds,
but I can never see any.

38:41.529 --> 38:43.656
Oh! He'll give you candy now.

38:44.657 --> 38:45.533
What?

38:46.117 --> 38:48.661
You don't have to lie
to Dr. V anymore.

38:49.537 --> 38:51.247
You can tell him the truth.

38:51.373 --> 38:52.749
He'll give it to you now.

38:53.875 --> 38:55.585
Are you working for him?

38:57.504 --> 38:59.464
Have you been spying on me?

39:00.090 --> 39:00.924
No.

39:00.924 --> 39:03.134
Is that why he's giving you drugs?

39:03.885 --> 39:05.845
To get information out of me?

39:05.845 --> 39:08.348
Don't be silly. I'm your friend!

39:09.516 --> 39:11.726
We're gonna have
so much fun together, too.

39:11.726 --> 39:14.813
We can celebrate holidays
and birthdays.

39:14.813 --> 39:17.482
Mine's in February,
which makes me an Aquarius.

39:21.319 --> 39:22.612
Wait.

39:37.627 --> 39:39.921
I told you I'm fucking innocent.

39:52.183 --> 39:53.059
Sofia?

39:55.895 --> 39:56.896
Sofia?

40:09.617 --> 40:10.910
Thank God you're okay.

40:17.375 --> 40:18.501
I'm glad you called me.

40:23.298 --> 40:24.382
Not too fast.

40:28.928 --> 40:30.472
I'm gonna get you something to eat.

40:31.973 --> 40:33.975
If you wanna get cleaned up,
there's a towel

40:33.975 --> 40:36.353
and a change of clothes
in the guest bath upstairs.

40:42.817 --> 40:44.319
Breakfast is almost ready.

41:17.602 --> 41:18.561
How you feeling?

41:23.108 --> 41:24.234
Like an idiot.

41:27.404 --> 41:28.363
I trusted him...

41:29.114 --> 41:31.449
when everything in my body
told me not to.

41:34.035 --> 41:36.246
I should have killed him
when I had the chance.

41:36.246 --> 41:37.205
Sofia...

41:37.205 --> 41:39.040
Now I don't even know
where the hell Oz is.

41:39.040 --> 41:41.501
I have no allies, no resources,

41:41.501 --> 41:44.212
and if I'm not on a plane
to Sicily by tomorrow...

41:44.921 --> 41:46.673
my Uncle Luca...

41:49.509 --> 41:50.593
Well...

41:53.638 --> 41:54.806
Maybe you should go.

41:58.768 --> 42:00.020
Not for your family.

42:00.520 --> 42:01.438
For yourself.

42:02.439 --> 42:04.816
Sofia, you've only been
out of Arkham a few weeks.

42:06.026 --> 42:07.569
You deserve a fresh start,

42:08.236 --> 42:09.571
an opportunity to heal.

42:10.113 --> 42:11.239
Why are you doing this?

42:12.240 --> 42:13.324
What do you want?

42:13.908 --> 42:14.826
To help you.

42:16.911 --> 42:17.996
And to feel better...

42:17.996 --> 42:20.331
or less guilty
for what happened to you.

42:20.331 --> 42:21.624
You quit.

42:22.959 --> 42:23.835
You abandoned me.

42:23.835 --> 42:24.919
I left because I had to,

42:25.503 --> 42:26.463
because I could.

42:27.672 --> 42:29.049
I know you didn't have that choice,

42:29.049 --> 42:30.050
but I'm here now.

42:32.218 --> 42:34.054
You don't have to pretend with me.

42:35.597 --> 42:37.849
You miss how it was
at Arkham, don't you?

42:39.601 --> 42:40.727
You've had a long night.

42:43.063 --> 42:44.606
The control that you had...

42:45.607 --> 42:46.608
treating me,

42:47.901 --> 42:49.611
rehabilitating me.

42:50.487 --> 42:51.821
I helped Alberto get you out.

42:53.907 --> 42:55.033
And now, here I am...

42:56.576 --> 42:57.952
wearing your clothes.

42:59.204 --> 43:01.456
I haven't forgotten, you know?

43:02.832 --> 43:04.250
The way you looked at me.

43:06.336 --> 43:07.504
So curious.

43:10.256 --> 43:11.549
What did it feel like?

43:12.133 --> 43:15.428
To get to watch a person unravel?

43:16.763 --> 43:19.265
And now, you're numbing yourself
as punishment.

43:21.309 --> 43:22.394
That's absurd.

43:25.188 --> 43:26.940
My father told me I was sick.

43:29.651 --> 43:30.902
And Dr. Ventris.

43:32.529 --> 43:34.239
And then the doctor after him.

43:35.949 --> 43:37.534
And then the doctor after him.

43:39.911 --> 43:41.705
For ten years,

43:42.872 --> 43:45.667
men have lied to me.

43:47.752 --> 43:48.920
And then I come home,

43:50.130 --> 43:51.214
and it's all the same.

43:54.467 --> 43:55.719
They think I'm broken.

43:57.846 --> 43:58.888
I'm not broken.

44:01.808 --> 44:03.351
I'm not the one who's sick.

44:06.730 --> 44:07.897
And neither are you.

44:12.569 --> 44:13.737
The world is.

44:24.122 --> 44:25.123
You're right.

44:26.082 --> 44:27.500
I deserve a fresh start.

44:34.257 --> 44:35.633
I do want some cheese.

44:35.633 --> 44:37.344
You know what?
I don't want any cheese.

44:37.344 --> 44:38.553
You hold the cheese.

45:23.765 --> 45:25.350
What the hell are you doin'?

45:25.350 --> 45:26.976
Supporting Uncle Luca.

45:27.852 --> 45:29.062
Same as you.

45:29.062 --> 45:30.355
Can you pass the meatballs?

45:40.198 --> 45:43.743
I'd like to express my gratitude
to everyone here.

45:43.743 --> 45:45.912
Tensions are high,

45:45.912 --> 45:49.165
and I wish we was gathered
under different circumstances.

45:49.165 --> 45:52.877
But our Family
has weathered storms before,

45:52.877 --> 45:55.088
and it has only made us stronger.

45:56.423 --> 45:57.507
Gia.

45:57.507 --> 45:58.758
But here, this house,

45:58.758 --> 46:01.928
us, we are each other's sanctuary,

46:01.928 --> 46:05.682
finding solace and celebration
even in our darkest hour.

46:06.349 --> 46:09.519
My brother used to say
that true strength--

46:13.481 --> 46:15.316
Forgive me. I've never been one
for speeches,

46:15.316 --> 46:16.985
but I did wanna say a few words.

46:17.485 --> 46:20.071
You don't mind, do you, Uncle Luca?

46:27.787 --> 46:28.621
Wow.

46:30.874 --> 46:32.167
Look at everyone.

46:32.709 --> 46:34.461
I believe the last time
we were all together

46:34.461 --> 46:37.464
was my father's birthday
10 years ago.

46:38.089 --> 46:39.924
I'm sure you all remember that night.

46:42.385 --> 46:43.678
I know I do.

46:43.678 --> 46:45.388
Come on. It's time for bed.

46:45.388 --> 46:47.307
But Daddy said there'd be cake.

46:47.307 --> 46:48.600
Take a seat, Carla.

46:54.689 --> 46:56.733
Gia, go get ready for bed, okay?

47:02.072 --> 47:03.114
As you all know,

47:05.408 --> 47:07.994
I was stuffed
in Arkham State Hospital

47:07.994 --> 47:09.412
for a decade...

47:10.413 --> 47:14.209
convicted of murdering seven women.

47:15.919 --> 47:17.087
Summer Gleeson,

47:17.796 --> 47:19.339
Taylor Montgomery,

47:19.339 --> 47:21.174
Yolanda Jones,

47:21.174 --> 47:22.717
Nancy Hoffman,

47:22.717 --> 47:24.260
Susanna Weakley,

47:24.928 --> 47:26.554
Devri Blake,

47:26.554 --> 47:28.139
and Tricia Becker.

47:29.182 --> 47:30.809
Their names are worth saying.

47:32.602 --> 47:34.813
Victims are so quickly forgotten,

47:34.813 --> 47:36.231
aren't they?

47:36.856 --> 47:40.110
Our stories are... rarely told.

47:40.110 --> 47:42.862
Okay, all right, I think that's--

47:45.073 --> 47:45.907
Yes?

47:51.246 --> 47:53.289
I've had a lot of time to reflect.

47:55.250 --> 47:56.501
And I have to say...

47:58.795 --> 48:00.880
I was genuinely surprised

48:01.631 --> 48:04.426
at how many of you wrote letters

48:04.426 --> 48:06.720
telling the judge
that I was mentally ill,

48:07.262 --> 48:08.596
like my mother.

48:09.305 --> 48:11.391
Not that the judge
needed much convincing.

48:11.391 --> 48:13.059
My father saw to that.

48:13.601 --> 48:16.271
Still, I trusted you.

48:19.983 --> 48:21.067
I loved you.

48:23.445 --> 48:25.864
And yet, not one of you...

48:27.323 --> 48:29.826
tried to help me.

48:31.703 --> 48:33.496
Except for my brother,

48:34.372 --> 48:37.000
the man you all flew in to mourn.

48:38.251 --> 48:42.088
And you know,
the real thorn in my side

48:42.088 --> 48:44.674
is that, unlike everyone here...

48:46.718 --> 48:48.261
I was innocent.

48:49.095 --> 48:50.013
I mean...

48:52.057 --> 48:54.601
Jesus Christ, Milos has
a higher body count than I do.

48:55.185 --> 48:56.061
Sofia!

49:00.523 --> 49:03.026
I know you're all anxious
for me to leave.

49:05.779 --> 49:07.614
No one has been shy about that.

49:11.451 --> 49:13.703
I'd really hoped
that it would be different.

49:15.121 --> 49:16.498
But I understand.

49:20.293 --> 49:22.587
I don't fit into this family anymore.

49:24.422 --> 49:26.841
So, tomorrow,
I'm starting a new life.

49:27.884 --> 49:29.010
For the first time,

49:29.761 --> 49:30.970
I have hope.

49:35.934 --> 49:38.061
To new beginnings.

49:40.271 --> 49:41.189
Cent'anni.

50:37.078 --> 50:38.913
Are you ready for some cake?

50:40.290 --> 50:42.709
I have a corner piece
with your name on it.

50:42.709 --> 50:44.252
It's extra chocolatey,

50:44.252 --> 50:46.504
with tons of frosting.

50:48.381 --> 50:49.215
But...

50:50.342 --> 50:52.385
we have to eat it in the greenhouse.

50:52.385 --> 50:53.720
Should we tell my mom?

50:54.346 --> 50:56.014
No. We don't need to wake her up.

50:57.098 --> 50:59.267
It can be our little secret, okay?

51:02.896 --> 51:04.356
Would you like some more?

51:04.356 --> 51:06.024
I should go to bed.

51:09.110 --> 51:13.782
You know, my brother and I
used to sleep out here

51:14.407 --> 51:15.575
when we were little.

51:16.993 --> 51:19.996
We would snuggle up in blankets,

51:19.996 --> 51:23.583
and we would pretend
that this was a jungle.

51:26.378 --> 51:28.171
Should we sleep out here tonight?

51:28.838 --> 51:30.298
That could be fun, right?

51:35.512 --> 51:38.181
My mom told me not to talk to you.

51:38.181 --> 51:40.475
She said you did bad things.

51:41.476 --> 51:42.644
She's right.

51:44.437 --> 51:46.398
I did do bad things.

51:47.107 --> 51:47.982
Why?

51:49.275 --> 51:53.029
Well, my father locked me away
in a dungeon

51:53.029 --> 51:55.949
with a bunch
of scary monsters, and...

51:56.741 --> 51:59.911
I had to fight them to survive.

52:03.248 --> 52:05.000
Am I gonna get locked away?

52:05.000 --> 52:07.919
No. You don't have
to worry about that.

52:09.295 --> 52:10.338
I'm gonna make sure

52:10.880 --> 52:13.216
that you never have
to fight any monsters.

52:13.842 --> 52:14.968
Okay?

52:16.886 --> 52:18.263
Now, get some sleep.

52:43.580 --> 52:44.998
Go back to sleep.

52:45.623 --> 52:47.000
I'll be right back.

55:28.328 --> 55:29.704
Put your pants on, Johnny.

55:31.164 --> 55:32.332
We need to talk.
